      "title": "Dividend increased to ₹25.00",
      "body": "Dividend of ₹25.00 is 400% higher than last year. Ex-date: 30th July 2026 Payment date: 5th September 2026 Dividend yield will be 2.2%, which is higher than the industry average of 0.4%. Sustainability & Growth Dividend is well covered by both earnings (5% earnings payout ratio) and cash flows (9% cash payout ratio). The dividend has decreased over the past 10 years, indicating a lack of growth and stability in payments. The company's earnings per share (EPS) would need to decline by 94% to shift the payout ratio to a potentially unsustainable range, which is more than the 5.7% EPS decline seen over the last 5 years.",
